## Task 12: Compact "payment received" toast variant + SSE trigger

Add a smaller toast variant for payment-received events and fire it (with the success chime) when a transaction completes.

### Existing pieces you'll use:
- `client/src/components/notification-system.tsx` — exports `NotificationProvider`, `useNotifications()` (gives `{ addNotification }`). `addNotification(n)` takes `{ type, title, message, duration, ... }`. Contains `interface Notification {...}`, `const TYPE_CONFIG`, and `function NotificationCard({ notification, onRemove })`. The success type accent is teal `#13C29A`. The full card surface is a navy gradient.
- `client/src/lib/sound.ts` — exports `playPaymentChime()` (interaction-gated, mute-aware; safe to call anytime).
- `client/src/lib/sse-client.ts` — exports `sseClient` with `.subscribe(eventType, cb)` and `.unsubscribe(eventType, cb)`. Payment completion arrives as event type `"transaction_updated"` with `message.transaction` whose `.status === "completed"`.
- `client/src/pages/merchant-terminal-mobile-v2.tsx` — already calls `sseClient.connect(merchantId)`, `sseClient.subscribe("transaction_updated", ...)`, and near line ~156 calls `useDeviceStatusMonitoring()` and `useSSEConnectionMonitoring(merchantId ?? 0)`.

### Step 1 — Extend the Notification interface (notification-system.tsx)
Add two optional fields to `interface Notification`:
```tsx
  compact?: boolean;   // render the small payment-received layout
  amount?: string;     // preformatted amount shown in the compact variant
```
(Note: `addNotification` takes `Omit<Notification,"id">`, so these flow through automatically.)

### Step 2 — Add a compact render branch in NotificationCard
In `function NotificationCard(...)`, AFTER `cfg`/`Icon` are computed but BEFORE the normal `return (...)`, add an early return for compact toasts:
```tsx
  if (notification.compact) {
    return (
      <div className="relative rounded-[16px] overflow-hidden"
        style={{
          background: "linear-gradient(150deg, rgba(4,13,109,0.97) 0%, rgba(7,20,90,0.96) 100%)",
          backdropFilter: "blur(24px) saturate(1.6)", WebkitBackdropFilter: "blur(24px) saturate(1.6)",
          border: "1px solid rgba(88,171,255,0.22)", boxShadow: "0 12px 36px rgba(4,13,109,0.45)",
        }}>
        <div className="flex items-center gap-2.5 px-3.5 py-2.5">
          <div className="flex-shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center"
            style={{ backgroundColor: `${cfg.color}1a`, border: `1px solid ${cfg.color}30` }}>
            <Icon className="w-3.5 h-3.5" style={{ color: cfg.color }} />
          </div>
          <span className="text-white text-sm font-semibold leading-none">{notification.title}</span>
          {notification.amount && (
            <span className="ml-auto text-sm font-bold leading-none" style={{ color: cfg.color }}>{notification.amount}</span>
          )}
        </div>
      </div>
    );
  }
```
Make sure this is placed where `cfg` and `Icon` are already defined (read the function to confirm the variable names — `cfg = TYPE_CONFIG[...]`, `Icon = cfg.icon`).

### Step 3 — Create the hook `client/src/hooks/use-payment-received-toast.ts`
```ts
import { useEffect, useRef } from "react";
import { sseClient } from "@/lib/sse-client";
import { useNotifications } from "@/components/notification-system";
import { playPaymentChime } from "@/lib/sound";

/** Fires a compact "payment received" toast + chime when a transaction completes. */
export function usePaymentReceivedToast() {
  const { addNotification } = useNotifications();
  const seen = useRef<Set<string>>(new Set());

  useEffect(() => {
    const handler = (message: any) => {
      const tx = message?.transaction;
      if (!tx || tx.status !== "completed") return;
      const key = `${tx.id}:${tx.completedSplits ?? 0}`;
      if (seen.current.has(key)) return;
      seen.current.add(key);

      const cents = tx.amountReceivedCents ?? tx.amountCents ?? tx.totalCents ?? 0;
      const amount = "$" + (cents / 100).toLocaleString("en-NZ", { minimumFractionDigits: 2, maximumFractionDigits: 2 });
      addNotification({ type: "success", title: "Payment received", message: "", amount, compact: true, duration: 3500 } as any);
      playPaymentChime();
    };
    sseClient.subscribe("transaction_updated", handler);
    return () => sseClient.unsubscribe("transaction_updated", handler);
  }, [addNotification]);
}
```
Before finalizing the `cents` field: open `merchant-terminal-mobile-v2.tsx` or a transactions type to check what amount field a transaction actually carries (e.g. `amountCents`, `totalCents`, `amount`). Keep the `??` fallback chain but order it so the real field is included. Report what field(s) you found.

### Step 4 — Mount the hook in the merchant terminal
In `client/src/pages/merchant-terminal-mobile-v2.tsx`, add `import { usePaymentReceivedToast } from "@/hooks/use-payment-received-toast";` and call `usePaymentReceivedToast();` next to the existing `useDeviceStatusMonitoring();` / `useSSEConnectionMonitoring(...)` calls (~line 156). (The component is already inside the NotificationProvider tree — confirm by checking that `useDeviceStatusMonitoring` which also uses `useNotifications` is called here without error.)

### Step 5 — Verify build
`npx vite build` → succeeds.

### Step 6 — Commit
```bash
git add client/src/components/notification-system.tsx client/src/hooks/use-payment-received-toast.ts client/src/pages/merchant-terminal-mobile-v2.tsx
git commit -m "feat(notifications): compact payment-received toast on SSE"
```
End the commit message with this trailer on its own line:
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

## Report
Report: **Status:** DONE | DONE_WITH_CONCERNS | BLOCKED | NEEDS_CONTEXT, what you implemented, which transaction amount field(s) you found and used, confirmation the terminal is inside NotificationProvider, the build result, files changed, commit SHA, any concerns. If the NotificationProvider context isn't available where you mount the hook, or you can't confirm the amount field, report NEEDS_CONTEXT rather than guessing.

